    "assumptions": [
      "Depth follows the deprojected density (Prugniel & Simien 1997) of Kormendy et al.'s (2009) Table 1 major-axis Sérsic fit to NGC 4649: n = 5.36 (+0.38, -0.32), half-light radius 132.05 (+11.6, -9.3) arcsec, on an oblate spheroid whose axis is M60's minor axis (position angle 196.0 degrees: the major axis is at 106.0 degrees in Table 3, interpolated to the half-light radius between the rows at 125.507 and 138.569 arcsec) in the plane of the sky, axis ratio 0.797 (1 - 0.203, the ellipticity interpolated the same way). The survey image's light along each sight line is kept; only its depth comes from the prior. The intrinsic orientation is not measured.",
      "The prior ends at 5.251 half-light radii, where Kormendy et al.'s Table 3 profile of NGC 4649 stops (693.426 arcsec, 56.0 kpc at 16.7 Mpc); light beyond that spheroid is not drawn.",
      "The 2700 x 2700 px cutout is requested on M60's HyperLEDA position (PGC 42831: 190.916504, +11.552706) in a tangent projection, north up and east left, 0.385237 degrees wide (twice 693.426 arcsec, 0.5136 arcsec per px), so its registration is the request's.",
      "NOX removes stars; what it leaves is masked afterwards: 9 neighbouring galaxies from HyperLEDA PGC (Paturel et al. 2003, CDS VII/237: every galaxy with a D25 whose mask reaches the cutout) at 3 times their D25 radius, M87's rule; 4 from the 2MASS Extended Source Catalog (CDS VII/233), which sizes the galaxies HyperLEDA gives no D25, at 3 times their K-band 20 mag isophotal radius; and the 27 Gaia DR3 stars brighter than G = 15, whose haloes NOX leaves, at 45 arcsec for G = 11, scaled with brightness (a factor 10 in radius per 5 magnitudes). No mask reaches beyond nine tenths of its distance from M60's centre (chosen here), so every isophote keeps unmasked light. A masked pixel takes the median of the unmasked light on its own isophote (the ellipse through it with the measured axis ratio and position angle), never more than it held.",
      "Every pixel is clamped to the median of the 45 px square around it, so star haloes and small background galaxies that NOX and the masks leave are not spread through the spheroid.",
      "Black level per channel: the median of the cleaned cutout's four 135 px corners, red 0.024, green 0.024, blue 0.016 (6, 6 and 4 of 255).",
